{
  /* The desktop package cannot use the root tsconfig, which is why the root EXCLUDES it — and why
     nothing here was typechecked at all until an unbound identifier shipped through `bun run
     typecheck` unnoticed. CI runs this config as a second step for that reason.

     The cause is that electrobun's SDK is raw TypeScript, not declarations: Electrobun 2 projects
     `.ts` sources under `.hutch/devkit/api` and the `paths` below point straight at them, so
     importing the SDK pulls its sources into the program as first-class files. Neither `exclude`
     nor `skipLibCheck` keeps them out — see the root config for why — and under the root's
     `exactOptionalPropertyTypes` they emit errors we cannot fix in a dependency.

     ONE of the root's flags is genuinely blocked. Measured on the electrobun 2.0.1 devkit:

       exactOptionalPropertyTypes  → 15 errors across 7 devkit files (BrowserView 7, BrowserWindow 2,
                                     Updater 2, Utils, Tray, ContextMenu, ApplicationMenu). Ours: 7.
       noUncheckedIndexedAccess    → 0 errors in electrobun. Ours: 129, ~90% of them array indexing
                                     in tests (88 in window-manager.test.ts alone).

     So `noUncheckedIndexedAccess` is off for OUR debt, not for the dependency's, and re-enabling it
     is a bounded piece of work rather than a wait. Prefer narrowing this file back toward the root
     config over widening it, and re-measure before believing either number. */
  "compilerOptions": {
    "allowImportingTsExtensions": true,
    "lib": ["ESNext", "DOM"],
    "module": "ESNext",
    "moduleResolution": "bundler",
    "noEmit": true,
    "noFallthroughCasesInSwitch": true,
    "noImplicitOverride": true,

    /* Where `electrobun/*` resolves from. Electrobun 2 ships no SDK on npm — `electrobun
       prepare` copies the release's SDK trees into a generated `.hutch/devkit` sysroot (run
       `bun run --cwd packages/desktop sync`, or any build, which syncs implicitly). Hutch also
       writes `.hutch/devkit/tsconfig.json` with the full 46-entry path map, and the intended
       wiring is to `extends` it — but that file sets `baseUrl`, which TypeScript 7 removed, so
       extending it fails the whole project with TS5102. These three entries are the entire
       `electrobun` surface this package imports; add one here if a fourth is ever needed, and
       revisit the `extends` when Hutch stops emitting `baseUrl`. */
    "paths": {
      "electrobun": ["./.hutch/devkit/api/sdks/main/index.ts"],
      "electrobun/main": ["./.hutch/devkit/api/sdks/main/index.ts"],
      "electrobun/view": ["./.hutch/devkit/api/browser/index.ts"]
    },

    "resolveJsonModule": true,
    "skipLibCheck": true,
    "strict": true,
    "target": "ESNext",
    "types": ["bun-types"]
  },
  "include": ["src/**/*", "tests/**/*", "scripts/**/*", "../../types.d.ts"]
}
